    "bookends": {
      "first": {
        "speaker": 9,
        "line": 3,
        "text": "Once... when it was still early in the twenty-first century... there existed a prison in a sea of sand. All signs of life in this place had been destroyed by something terrible... and that something had dried up into the earth... and the earth was a prison for all mankind."
      },
      "last": {
        "speaker": 9,
        "line": 851,
        "text": "And then we were filled with a great and strange wisdom. We went to a place where we could bury our regret. That same regret that had imbedded itself, without choice, in the hearts of those who were no longer around to show us the way."
      }
    },
